	<Folder>
		<name>Yellowstone National Park</name>
		<open>1</open>
		<description><![CDATA[This folder has major points of interest among the countless here in the nation's first national park (established in 1872), divided into general areas. Most of the information is from the park's <a href="http://www.yellowstoneparknet.com/">website</a>. Of course there are thousands of trails and backcountry areas for the more adventurous as well as the major destinations included here - 99% of the park's 3,400 square miles (2.2 million acres) remain undeveloped.

Yellowstone offers an incredible variety of things to see and do with its natural beauty of mountains, rivers, canyons and lakes; fantastic geothermal activity in the form of geysers, hot springs, colorful pools and paint pots; and a vast variety of wildlife including bears, bison, elk, moose, antelope, bighorn sheep, mountain goats, wolves, coyotes, bobcats, deer, and the mythical jackelope. Unlike many wilderness areas, most visitors will see many of these creatures when visiting Yellowstone.]]></description>
		<View>
			<longitude>-110.3807032897736</longitude>
			<latitude>44.54338982886499</latitude>
			<range>132610.0960365903</range>
			<tilt>0</tilt>
			<heading>0.5067539834967845</heading>
		</View>
