			<Placemark>
				<name>North Entrance</name>
				<description>Near the town of Gardiner, Montana, this entrance provides a dramatic arrival to Yellowstone through the deep canyons leading into Mammoth Hot Springs area. This is the entrance with the famous brick arch and plaques reading &quot;For the benefit and enjoyment of the people&quot; and &quot;Created by act of Congress March 1, 1872&quot;.</description>
