		<Folder>
			<name>Other Campgrounds</name>
			<description>Most campgrounds are on a first-come, first-served basis and often fill up by noon during the busy summer season. Some areas allow only RV or trailers and prohibit tent camping due to the proximity of bears. 

When bears become a regular nuisance or hazard they are removed to remote areas of the park, but you could receive a visit from a black bear or grizzly at any time: this is their home, you are merely visiting. Pay attention to all instructions about food storage and bear safety - Yellowstone is bear country!</description>
