				</Point>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Upper Falls</name>
				<description>Upper Falls of the Yellowstone are 109 feet tall and carry 5,000 to 63,500 gallons per second of water down the Yellowstone River to Lower Falls and on to the Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone. 
Unfortunately perspective is lost in Keyhole: they are truly magnificent.</description>
