			<Placemark>
				<name>Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone</name>
				<description>The canyon proper is roughly 20 miles long. It varies from 800 to 1,200 feet deep and is 1,500 to 4,000 feet wide, ending in the spectacular Upper and Lower Falls of the Yellowstone River. 

Soaring over Yellowstone or perched high in their enormous five foot nests, live the osprey. Since the 1980&apos;s six to ten osprey nests have been seen in the canyon. Meadows and forests surround the canyon and offer habitat for other wildlife such as elk, moose, and bison.</description>
				<View>
					<longitude>-110.3461633694599</longitude>
					<latitude>44.84576727289254</latitude>
					<range>6706.757777993817</range>
					<tilt>68.76574755928789</tilt>
					<heading>156.3595866121137</heading>
				</View>
